# Keep the build context small and free of local state. Docker reads
# .dockerignore only from the context root, so this is the ONE file
# that applies once the build context is this whole repo -- the
# .dockerignore files that used to live in backend/ and frontend/ are
# now inert, and anything they excluded has to be listed again here.
#
# The highest-stakes entry below is frontend/public/config: it is
# gitignored, generated by `task dev:frontend`, and points the SPA at
# a developer's local backend. Never let it reach a production build.
#
# A pattern with no `**/` prefix only matches at the context root, not
# inside backend/ or frontend/ -- both submodules carry their own
# .git, .github and .devcontainer, so those three specifically need
# the recursive form or they leak straight through.

**/.git
**/.github
**/.devcontainer
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.task

# Local developer state and credentials -- never useful in an image.
.env
backend/.env
backend/dev-auth.json
backend/secret.key
backend/uploads
backend/logs
backend/dev-utilities

# Build output the image regenerates itself. Scoped to the exact path,
# not **/docs: backend/docs/source is the Sphinx source tree the image
# build actually needs.
backend/docs/build
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage

# Generated at dev time by the umbrella Taskfile and gitignored: it
# points the SPA at a developer's local backend. Must never be baked
# into an image.
frontend/public/config

# Nothing at the umbrella root is needed to build the image. Scoped to
# the root for the same reason as backend/docs/build above: docs and
# dev-utilities both also exist inside backend/, with different (and
# needed) contents.
.claude
docs
dev-utilities
*.md
handoff-vue-components.md
